INT8-G64 attention-backend integration for vLLM 0.27.1 / SM80
================================================================

This is the second half of the INT8-G64 integration; the cache dtype and the
KV-cache spec live in ``int8-g64-vllm.patch``, and the bridge module itself is
``int8_g64.py`` in this directory (installed as
``vllm/v1/attention/ops/int8_g64.py``).

Diffed from the pristine ``v1/attention/backends/triton_attn.py`` of the
qualified vLLM 0.27.1 tree to the version that was actually deployed and
measured.  It contains four separate changes, each of which was needed to get a
working run, and each of which is recorded with its evidence in handover
sections 21 and 23:

  1. route INT8-G64 prefill to the dedicated Triton kernel.  The stock
     ``unified_attention`` treats this mode as per-token-head and computes
     ``BLOCK_Q = BLOCK_M // num_queries_per_kv`` = ``16 // 0``, i.e. a
     ZeroDivisionError on every prefill and warmup call, and it cannot express
     per-group G=64 scales at all;
  2. allocate the E38 verify workspace for every split_count in ``__init__``
     instead of lazily keyed on ``(batch, split_count)``.  Warmup captures CUDA
     graphs for several capture sizes, so the lazy form allocated inside capture
     regions and replay then followed stale pointers (illegal memory access at
     ``run_fullgraph -> graphs[desc].replay()``);
  3. accept ``sliding_window is None`` as well as ``(-1, -1)`` in the E38 verify
     gate.  Full-attention layers report ``None``, so the strict test silently
     disabled the E38 path entirely and verify fell back to the prefill-shaped
     kernel (~2.7 tok/s whole-model at 4k);
  4. count the G64 prefill route's calls for the diagnostic in handover 21.7.

Apply from the vLLM site-package root:

  patch -p1 < bench/int8-g64/int8-g64-triton.patch

Note that this patch deliberately does NOT touch ``spec_decode_attn.py``: the
production control arm's split-KV verify kernel is a separate, already-tracked
patch series.

